WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.935
Mastery Starter 13.0.

00:00:02.935 --> 00:00:04.740
New to The Income Engine?

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:05.800
Start here.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.887
In about ten minutes, you'll go from

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:09.580
zero to ready for this module.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:13.470
Income from DeFi should be planned like a

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:16.245
pension, not chased like a jackpot: build it

00:00:16.245 --> 00:00:19.513
from durable sources, subtract the losses you should

00:00:19.513 --> 00:00:21.980
expect, and pay yourself less than that.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:25.390
Durability: how long and reliably

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.055
a source tends to pay.

00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:30.900
Risk-adjusted yield: yield minus expected losses.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.495
LGD: how much you lose

00:00:32.495 --> 00:00:34.460
if a loss event happens.

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:38.210
Payout ratio: share of expected income you take out.

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:41.350
Principal: the capital itself, never spent as income.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.385
Modules 0–12.

00:00:45.685 --> 00:00:47.762
Take one position and compute its

00:00:47.762 --> 00:00:50.145
risk-adjusted yield with the calculator

00:00:51.445 --> 00:00:54.675
Beginner: Ranks income sources by durability.

00:00:54.675 --> 00:01:00.005
Practitioner: Builds an income portfolio with risk-adjusted expected income.

00:01:00.005 --> 00:01:03.078
Master: Runs a payout policy that survives bad

00:01:03.078 --> 00:01:06.020
years, with annual reviews and scaling rules.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.513
You've mastered this module when your payout is set

00:01:10.513 --> 00:01:14.504
below risk-adjusted expected income and never draws on principal.

00:01:15.804 --> 00:01:18.319
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:01:18.319 --> 00:01:23.169
Next up, Lesson 13.1: Income sources ranked by durability.
